<title>FINLAND: ASPO SEES UPTURN, BUT WEAKER '96 EARNINGS.</title>
<headline>ASPO SEES UPTURN, BUT WEAKER '96 EARNINGS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Aspoyhtyma Oy said in a statement on Wednesday it expected earnings to improve during the end of the year, but full-year 1996 earnings would remain below last year's.</p>
<p>&quot;Earnings are expected to continue improving as the year end approaches, but to fall below the 1995 figures,&quot; Aspo said in its January-August interim report.</p>
<p>In 1995, group profit before extraordinary items and tax was 97.5 million markka.</p>
</text>
